# Session cookies - never commit (these ARE live login credentials).
# The whole auth/ directory is ignored so a new platform's state file is
# covered the moment it is created, without anyone remembering to add it.
auth/
# A JAR THAT HAS BEEN COPIED ASIDE IS STILL A JAR, and the narrow pattern did
# not know that: `*_auth.json` missed tiktok_auth.CLOBBERED-204011.json.bak, so
# a destroyed-session backup sat in the tree untracked AND UNIGNORED - one
# `git add -A` from being committed with its cookies. Note the second pattern is
# the one that catches it: the name is `tiktok_auth` + `.CLOBBERED-204011` +
# `.json.bak`, so the substring `_auth.json` never appears and a mere trailing
# wildcard is not enough. Between them these cover the suffixes people actually
# produce - .bak, .old, .orig, .1, and a dated copy.
#
# Deliberately NOT `*_auth*`, which would also swallow collectors/build_*_auth.py
# - already-tracked files are unaffected, but the NEXT one added would be
# silently ignored, which is a worse bug than the one being fixed.
*_auth.json*
*_auth.*.json*
data/facebook/fb_auth.json
data/instagram/ig_auth.json
data/linkedin/linkedin_auth.json
# Persistent TikTok browser profile (device-bound session + solved-CAPTCHA
# state) - live credentials, same as the *_auth.json files above. One dir per
# OS user (tiktok_profile_<user>/), so match the prefix.
data/tiktok/tiktok_profile_*/
data/tiktok/tiktok_profile/
# Per-CONNECTION persistent browser profiles (data/<platform>/browser_profiles/
# <connection>/). Exactly the same live, device-bound session state as the
# directories above - one per connected account instead of one per OS user - so
# it is ignored on the same terms. Matched under any platform's data dir,
# because the layout is the collector-wide one rather than TikTok's alone.
data/*/browser_profiles/
# Comment-batch checkpoints (data/<platform>/resume/). Operational state, not a
# demo artifact: they hold collected comments for one connected account, they
# are rewritten every video, and they are worthless to anyone but the machine
# that made them.
data/*/resume/
# The MOBILE API's device identity (data/tiktok/tiktok_device_<user>.json and
# data/tiktok/devices/<connection>.json). This is what a run PRESENTS to
# TikTok's app API - device_id, install id, openudid, cdid - so it is identity
# material of exactly the kind a cookie jar is, and it is treated the same way:
# 0600 on disk, in no log, no run output and no API response, and never here.
data/*/tiktok_device_*.json
data/*/devices/
# Challenge diagnostics: a URL, a title and (only when
# TIKTOK_DIAGNOSTIC_SCREENSHOTS is set) a screenshot of the page that blocked a
# run. No cookie or token is ever written here, but a screenshot of a logged-in
# page can show an account name, so it stays out of the repository.
data/*/diagnostics/
# Persistent X browser profile (login/verification state) - live credentials,
# same as the *_auth.json files above. One dir per OS user.
data/x/x_profile_*/
data/x/x_auth.json
# Persistent Threads browser profile (login_threads.py --interactive). The
# session itself is OPTIONAL for this platform - the collector scrapes
# anonymously - but when one exists it is live credentials like any other.
data/threads/threads_profile_*/
data/threads/threads_auth.json
# Persistent Facebook browser profile (login_facebook.py). Live credentials,
# same as the *_auth.json files above. One dir per OS user.
data/facebook/fb_profile_*/

# Run storage - never commit. storage/ also matches actor-platform/storage/
# (run directories, logs, outputs), and old local Apify runs left a root
# storage/ whose INPUT.json may hold cookies. .fb_groups_work/ is the groups
# service's per-run auth staging + per-worker temp data dirs (seeded with a
# copy of fb_auth.json).
storage/
.fb_groups_work/

# Loose credential files. A live Anthropic key was committed as
# "ANTHROPIC API KEY sk ant.txt" (removed 2026-09-05); the key belongs in .env,
# which is already ignored above. These patterns stop the next one.
*API*KEY*.txt
*api*key*.txt
*.key
*secret*.txt

# COLLECTED DATA AND REPORTS STAY OUT OF GIT. The demo build writes synthetic
# data here, but a real collector's output would hold real people's posts,
# names and comments, so the rule stays. Field templates live in fixtures/demo/.
data/**/*.json
data/**/*.jsonl
reports/output/*
